# Vercel Web Analytics Installation

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for the Personal Deal Scout Next.js application.

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- **Added**: `@vercel/analytics` v2.0.1 to dependencies in `package.json`
- Installed using npm with `--legacy-peer-deps` flag to resolve peer dependency conflicts
- Updated `package-lock.json` to reflect the new dependency

### 2. Analytics Component Integration
- **Modified**: `src/app/layout.tsx`
  - Added import: `import { Analytics } from "@vercel/analytics/next";`
  - Added `<Analytics />` component to the root layout body, alongside the existing `<SpeedInsights />` component

## Implementation Details

Following the official Vercel Analytics documentation (fetched from https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart), I implemented the Next.js App Router setup:

1. **Framework Detection**: Identified the project uses Next.js App Router (based on `src/app/layout.tsx`)
2. **Package Manager**: Detected npm as the package manager (based on `package-lock.json`)
3. **Installation**: Used npm with legacy peer deps flag to handle dependency resolution
4. **Integration**: Added the Analytics component to the root layout following the documented pattern for Next.js App Router

## Verification

All verification steps completed successfully:

✅ **Build**: Production build completed successfully (16.2s TypeScript compilation, 12 static pages generated)
✅ **Linter**: ESLint passed with no errors
✅ **Tests**: All 305 tests in 75 test files passed
✅ **Dependencies**: Lock file updated correctly

## Files Modified

- `package.json` - Added @vercel/analytics dependency
- `package-lock.json` - Updated with new package and dependencies
- `src/app/layout.tsx` - Added Analytics import and component

## Notes

- The Analytics component is placed in the root layout alongside the existing SpeedInsights component
- Both Vercel integrations (Analytics and Speed Insights) are now active in the application
- Analytics will track page views automatically once deployed to Vercel
- No additional configuration is required; analytics data will be available in the Vercel dashboard after deployment

## Next Steps

Once deployed to Vercel, the Web Analytics dashboard will automatically start collecting data including:
- Page views and unique visitors
- Top pages and referrers
- Device and browser information
- Geographic data
